# ---- Other people's copyrighted material: on the bench PC, never committed -------------------------------------
# Vendor datasheets (PDF) and their text.  tools/jlc_datasheet.py (by LCSC code) and tools/adi_datasheet.py fetch
# them again; the documents cite them as datasheets/<file>.pdf, build/txt/<part>.txt and docs/datasheets/txt/.
/datasheets/
/docs/datasheets/
/build/txt/
# ... and the copies the design reviewers made of them: PDFs, text, renders of their pages
/design_review/Claude/txt/
/design_review/Grok4.7/ds/
/design_review/Grok4.7/img/
/design_review/Gemini3.8Flash/*.png
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/ADL5375.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/ADL5380.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/HMC536.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/LP5907.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/MAX2871.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/SN74LVC1G3157.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/THS4541.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/TLV3601.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/TPS7A20.txt
/design_review/GPT-5.6Terra/TS5A3159.txt
/design_review/KimiK3/ad5696r.txt
/design_review/KimiK3/balun_crop.png
/design_review/KimiK3/balun_ds-1.png
/design_review/KimiK3/sky-5.png
/design_review/KimiK3/sky-6.png
# TUL's board files for the PYNQ-Z2 and its product photo (gateware/README.md says where they come from)
/gateware/pynq/board_files/
# The SMA and MMCX jacks' 3D models, converted from EasyEDA's.  gen/library.py copies them into hardware/lib/
# when they are here, and reports them missing when they are not; nothing but the 3D view uses them.
/gen/vendored/MMCX-TH_BWMMCX-KE.wrl
/gen/vendored/SMA-TH_5P-L14.5-W6.0-H9.6_BWSMA-KWE-Z001.wrl
/hardware/lib/CostasLink.3dshapes/MMCX-TH_BWMMCX-KE.wrl
/hardware/lib/CostasLink.3dshapes/SMA-TH_5P-L14.5-W6.0-H9.6_BWSMA-KWE-Z001.wrl
# JLCPCB's parts data and EasyEDA's land patterns, cached by tools/jlc_api.py and mfg/footprint_check.py:
# theirs, and fetched again when stale.  JLCPCB's production-file confirmation zips (their CAM output, 17 MB each).
/tools/jlc_cache.json
/mfg/jlc_footprint_cache.json
*_gerbers_Y*.zip

# ---- The bench's record -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The bench's full record stays on the bench PC: only code, docs and a few examples go to git (Jason, 2026-10-31)
bringup/data/*
!bringup/data/examples/
# the VNA's Touchstone files and level tables are kept (they took real work: Jason, 2026-11-03); their plots are
# made again from them (vna_measure.py plot, vna_tests.py tdr), and the soaks' records stay out
!bringup/data/board_A/
bringup/data/board_A/*
!bringup/data/board_A/vna/
bringup/data/board_A/vna/*.png
bringup/data/board_A/vna/*_INVALID*
# (bringup/data/board_A/photos/ holds the phone's originals of photos/, with their metadata)
bringup/.locks/

# ---- Working notes exchanged with Claude (the chat logs are the record) ------------------------------------------
/QUESTIONS.md
/ANSWERS.md

# ---- Build intermediates ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ignored, except what the documents cite or a reviewer needs (DESIGN_REVIEW_PROMPT.md section 6): the numbers,
# the placement, the routing, the cost, the link rates, the pin audit.  The rest of build/ is remade by build.py,
# the gateware Makefile and pynq/build.tcl (whose reports name the machine's paths); the board renders the
# documents show are copied to docs/images/.
/build/*
!/build/COST_ESTIMATE.md
!/build/link_rates.md
!/build/constellations.txt
!/build/scratch/
/build/scratch/*
!/build/scratch/pin_audit.md
!/build/budget.json
!/build/link_rates.json
!/build/constellations.json
!/build/cost.json
!/build/placement.json
!/build/route_report.json
!/build/trajectories.json
!/build/hosts.json
!/build/hosts_knobs.json
!/build/latency_roadmap.json
!/build/optics_roadmap.json
!/build/wifi_channels.json
!/build/system_budget.json
# A reviewer's private copy of the tree (DESIGN_REVIEW_PROMPT.md section 0.3)
/design_review/*/repo/
# Vivado's strays beside wherever it was launched (pynq/build.tcl removes NA/ itself)
/gateware/NA/
/gateware/.Xil/
/gateware/*.jou
/gateware/vivado*.log

# ---- Tools' droppings -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# KiCad: per-session locks, stray DRC/ERC temporaries, its autosave history (a git repo of its own)
fp-info-cache
*-backups
*.lck
tmp*.rpt
.history/
# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.DS_Store
